    "updated_at": "2025-08-20T23:29:25Z",
    "body": "Does output's for attribute *actually* do anything? I can see it's [specced](https://www.w3.org/TR/html-aam/#att-for-output) to sometimes affect AT mappings but WebKit doesn't seem to do anything for it (Even for the linux ports using ATSPI)?\n\nPotentially it could be omitted if it's not actually useful at all, but given it exists and isn't deprecated I guess completeness makes sense?\n\nAt least in WebKit the implementation for .formElement is also non-trivial, label.forElement is however a simple change to make. Haven't investigated the .headerElements stuff yet.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
