    "updated_at": "2025-09-11T16:02:58Z",
    "body": "> Can you expand on this? I don't understand how cross-root or referenceTarget would prevent us from, e.g., returning null if pointing to elements of the wrong type.\n\nI'll be honest I slightly mis-remembered how some of this worked. We can nullify the returned value if it's \"invalid\", but the type of the property would have to be `HTMLElement?` (or potentially even `Element?`)",
