    "updated_at": "2025-09-12T07:52:26Z",
    "body": "For my 2c on validation: having chatted with Luke a bit about this, I think I'd lean towards _not_ validating the reflected attributes other than checking they reflect the _attr_-associated element (not always equivalent to the labelled element, etc).\n\n- I think of the reflected attributes as a piece of data, approximately equivalent to the associated content attribute.\n- With custom elements and reference target, we (unfortunately) can't limit the reflected attributes by type: the getter might well return a custom element rather than an `HTMLListElement` or whatever.\n- So, I think the most useful thing is to return the relevant piece of data, which is the _attr_-associated element (where relevant, retargeted to the appropriate scope); this is analogous to `getAttribute()`. ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
