    "updated_at": "2025-09-15T12:13:28Z",
    "body": "Yeah so the reference target PR does update .control for example to handle the new behaviour. But they're still readonly.\n\nAs for the dynamic question I'll let Alice answer but I think the answer is that yes .control will return null until the reference target is setup and valid (because control is limited to situations where a valid labelable element is referenced)\n\nIf we added a .forElement that did the reflection the question then depends on if that is limited to just labelable elements.\n\nI personally think we should leave existing properties as readonly and add new ones for read/write reflection, for naming consistency and they could either do validation or not, popoverTargetElement as precedent *doesn't* restrict to elements with a popover attribute.",
