    "created_at": "2025-09-15T18:56:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-15T18:57:58Z",
    "body": "> You can setup a relationship before the custom element is initialized and has a reference target. Would it return null in that case until the custom element is initialized?\n\nIt depends on what we decide about validation, and when the reference target is set relative to when the element it refers to is added.\n\nAssuming there is no validation for the IDL attributes beyond checking that the target is a valid attr-associated element (`for`-associated in this case), then we would have something like:\n\n```html\n<label for=custom>Name</label>\n<custom-input id=\"custom\"><!-- shadow dom contents not yet added, and no reference target set --></custom-input>\n\n<script>\nlabel.forElement == custom;\nlabel.control == null;       // `custom` is not a labelable element\n\nlet shadow = custom.attachShadow();\nshadow.referenceTarget = \"real-input\";\n\nlabel.forElement == null;    // invalid reference target -> no for-associated element\nlabel.control == null;\n\nlet input = document.createElement(\"input\");\ninput.id = \"real-input\";\nshadow.appendChild(input); \n\nlabel.forElement == custom;  // the for-associated element is `input`\nlabel.control == custom;     // the labelled control is also `input`\n</script>\n```\n\nFor implicit label association:\n\n```html\n<label>Name\n  <custom-input id=\"custom\"><!-- shadow dom contents not yet added, and no reference target set --></custom-input>\n</label>\n\n<script>\nlabel.forElement == null;    // no `for`-associated element since there's no `for` attribute\nlabel.control == null;       // `custom` is not a labelable element\n\nlet shadow = custom.attachShadow();\nshadow.referenceTarget = \"real-input\";\n\nlabel.forElement == null;    // still no `for` attribute\nlabel.control == null;       // still not labelable\n\nlet input = document.createElement(\"input\");\ninput.id = \"real-input\";\nshadow.appendChild(input); \n\nlabel.forElement == null;    // still no `for` attribute\nlabel.control == custom;     // the labelled control is `input`\n</script>\n```\n\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
